<article class="env-lemma" id="0E6F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E6F">Lemma <span data-tag="0E6F">109.4.3</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a family of curves. Then there exists an étale covering $\{ S_ i \to S\} $ such that $X_ i = X \times _ S S_ i$ is a scheme. We may even assume $X_ i$ is H-projective over $S_ i$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is an immediate corollary of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DQ0" data-tag="0DQ0">109.4.2</a>. Namely, unwinding the definitions, this lemma gives there is a surjective smooth morphism $S' \to S$ such that $X' = X \times _ S S'$ comes endowed with an invertible $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-module $\mathcal{L}'$ which is ample on $X'/S'$. Then we can refine the smooth covering $\{ S' \to S\} $ by an étale covering $\{ S_ i \to S\} $, see More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/055V" data-tag="055V">37.38.7</a>. After replacing $S_ i$ by a suitable open covering we may assume $X_ i \to S_ i$ is H-projective, see Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0B5N" data-tag="0B5N">29.44.6</a> and <a href="/tag/01WB" data-tag="01WB">29.44.4</a> (this is also discussed in detail in More on Morphisms, Section <a href="/tag/0B44" data-tag="0B44">37.50</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>